lina: Go snippet (trying to keep it minimal, placeholders used):
```go
// Go: connect to private endpoint via internal KMS proxy, load custom CA
package main

import (
  "crypto/tls"
  "crypto/x509"
  "io/ioutil"
  "os"
  "net/http"
  "github.com/redwood-inference/redwood-go"
)

func main() {
  os.Setenv("REDWOOD_ENDPOINT", "https://private.cluster.local:9701")
  os.Setenv("REDWOOD_KMS_PROXY", "https://kms-proxy.local:8200")
  // PKCS#11 HSM (env only, do not put PINs in code)
  os.Setenv("PKCS11_MODULE_PATH", "/usr/lib/pkcs11/libhsm.so")
  os.Setenv("PKCS11_TOKEN_LABEL", "my-hsm")

  caPem, _ := ioutil.ReadFile("/etc/ssl/private-ca.pem")
  roots := x509.NewCertPool()
  roots.AppendCertsFromPEM(caPem)
  tlsCfg := &tls.Config{RootCAs: roots} // TLS pinning in airgap
  httpClient := &http.Client{Transport: &http.Transport{TLSClientConfig: tlsCfg}}

  client := redwood.NewClient(&redwood.Config{HTTPClient: httpClient})
  resp, _ := client.Generate("verify connectivity")
  println(resp.Text)
}
```

lina: Node snippet (lightweight):
```js
// Node: use custom CA and proxy url placeholders
const {RedwoodClient} = require('@redwood/sdk')
const https = require('https')
const fs = require('fs')

process.env.REDWOOD_ENDPOINT = 'https://private.cluster.local:9701'
process.env.REDWOOD_KMS_PROXY = 'https://kms-proxy.local:8200'
// PKCS11 handled by host; set env vars PKCS11_MODULE_PATH / PKCS11_PIN externally

const ca = fs.readFileSync('/etc/ssl/private-ca.pem')
const agent = new https.Agent({ca})
const client = new RedwoodClient({agent})
; (async () => {
  const r = await client.generate('verify connectivity')
  console.log(r.text)
})()
```

sam: Security review notes: good structure. Please ensure: (1) NO hard-coded PINs/tokens in snippets (use $REDWOOD_TOKEN / {{KMS_PROXY_URL}} placeholders), (2) advise file perms (600) for private CA bundles, (3) call out that PKCS#11 env vars should be set on the host or via systemd unit, not in container images, (4) add a short line to link to the token rotation playbook after migration.

maria: Docs + ops nit: add an offline mirror checksum line and where to push the artifact in our private registry. Example to include: `sha256sum installer-offline-1.3.0.tar.gz` and `scp installer-offline-1.3.0.tar.gz private-registry:/var/mirrors/redwood/installer/`. Also drop a sample systemd unit snippet for a kms-proxy sidecar in airgap.

josh: tested the Go example in the airgap lab. Works after I mounted `/var/run/hsm` for the PKCS#11 device and pointed PKCS11_MODULE_PATH to the correct lib. One snag: our worker nodes couldn't reach 8200 outbound (blocked by egress firewall). Suggested note: either NAT egress or run the kms-proxy as a local sidecar.

lina: thanks. I'll add a short recommendation: preferred topology = kms-proxy sidecar (local) for fully isolated clusters, fallback = NAT egress + egress allowlist for 8200 and 443. Also will list ports used: 9701 (node<>engine), 8200 (kms-proxy), 443 (upstream mirrors) and 22 for artifact push.

